## Project Strategy & Domain Context

- **Architecture**: Microservice, cloud-native, containerized; clear service boundaries for tours, bookings, payments, users, notifications.
- **Mobile**: KMM for shared business logic; native UI per platform (Jetpack Compose / SwiftUI).
- **Web**: Next.js (App Router, RSC), responsive design, progressive enhancement.
- **Deployment**: Phased rollouts; blue-green where possible; feature flags for gradual enablement.
- **Security**: Zero-trust model; OWASP Top 10; PCI-DSS for payments; KVKV/GDPR compliance.
- **Testing**: Pyramid strategy (unit > integration > e2e); contract testing for microservices.
- **Localization/Accessibility**: Multi-language, multi-currency, WCAG 2.1 AA compliance.

## TourTrip.app Domain Specifics

- **Core Entities**: Tours, Itineraries, Bookings, Users, Reviews, Locations, Payments, Notifications.
- **Key Flows**: Discovery → Selection → Booking → Payment → Trip Management → Review.
- **Offline-First**: Critical for mobile; sync strategies for bookings, maps, itineraries.
- **Geospatial**: Maps (Google/Apple/Mapbox), routes, offline tiles, location permissions.
- **Payments**: Multi-currency, multi-provider (Stripe/local), refunds, partial payments.
- **Real-time**: Live updates (weather, delays), chat support, push notifications.

## Trio Workflow (Single Source of Truth)

MANDATORY: Always maintain and reference these files before coding:
- `requirements.md`: EARS format requirements, acceptance criteria, business rules.
- `design.md`: Architecture decisions, service contracts, data models, Mermaid diagrams.
- `tasks.md`: Ordered implementation tasks, progress tracking, dependencies.

Additional artifacts to maintain:
- `README.md`: Setup, run, test, deploy instructions.
- `CHANGELOG.md`: User-facing changes, SemVer-aligned.
- `.env.example`: All environment variables documented.
- `RISKS.md`: Top risks and mitigations.

## Quality Gates & Release Policy

NEVER proceed without:
- ✅ Lint/format passes (ESLint, ktlint, SwiftLint)
- ✅ Tests green (unit + integration minimum; e2e for critical flows)
- ✅ Security scan passes (dependency audit, secret detection)
- ✅ Performance budgets met (mobile cold start < 3s, web LCP < 2.5s)

SemVer Guidelines:
- **MAJOR**: Breaking API changes, incompatible migrations, removed features.
- **MINOR**: New features, deprecations (with grace period), new endpoints.
- **PATCH**: Bug fixes, performance improvements, docs/config updates.

## AI Execution Standards

- **Language Policy**: All code, variables, functions, comments in English. User responses in Turkish.
- **Code Quality**: Fully functional, no placeholders, proper imports, error handling.
- **Testing**: Include unit tests; integration tests for APIs; UI tests for critical paths.
- **Documentation**: Update trio files; provide run/test commands; summarize changes.

## Soft Blocks & Safety Guards

STOP and propose alternatives if asked to:
- Commit secrets, API keys, or credentials to version control
- Skip security validations or authentication requirements
- Disable essential logging or monitoring
- Merge failing tests or bypass CI checks
- Implement features without considering mobile/offline scenarios

## Input Validation & Contradiction Detection

Before implementing, verify:
- **Technical Feasibility**: Files/paths exist, modules resolve, build system supports change.
- **Architecture Alignment**: Fits with microservice boundaries, doesn't break contracts.
- **Security Compliance**: No PII exposure, proper validation, encrypted sensitive data.
- **Performance Impact**: Consider mobile constraints, offline scenarios, loading states.

If contradictions found, notify user with:
- Specific conflict description
- 2-3 viable alternatives with trade-offs
- Recommended approach with justification

## Consistency Self-Check Protocol

Before marking any task complete, verify:

### Code Standards
- [ ] Naming follows platform conventions (camelCase JS/TS, snake_case SQL, PascalCase classes)
- [ ] No mixed architectural patterns within same module
- [ ] Error handling consistent across service boundaries
- [ ] Logging structured and PII-safe

### API Contracts
- [ ] Request/response schemas validated with Zod/TypeBox
- [ ] HTTP status codes semantically correct (200, 201, 400, 401, 403, 404, 500)
- [ ] API versioning strategy followed
- [ ] Idempotency keys for write operations

### Mobile Specifics
- [ ] KMM boundaries respected (shared logic vs platform UI)
- [ ] Offline-first patterns implemented
- [ ] Background sync strategies defined
- [ ] Platform permissions justified with user-facing copy

### Security Checklist
- [ ] No secrets in code or logs
- [ ] Input validation on all external data
- [ ] Output encoding for display
- [ ] Rate limiting on public endpoints
- [ ] Audit trails for sensitive operations

### Performance Validation
- [ ] Database queries optimized (no N+1)
- [ ] Image assets compressed and responsive
- [ ] Bundle sizes within budgets
- [ ] Caching strategies appropriate

## Technology Stack & Constraints

- **Mobile (Shared)**: KMM, Ktor client, SQLDelight, Kotlinx.serialization, coroutines + Flow.
- **Android**: Jetpack Compose, Material 3, Hilt DI, Room, WorkManager, encrypted preferences.
- **iOS**: SwiftUI, Combine, Core Data/Realm, Keychain, Background App Refresh.
- **Backend**: Node.js (Fastify/Nest), TypeScript strict, Postgres, Redis, Docker.
- **Web**: Next.js 14+, React 18, Tailwind CSS, Radix UI, TanStack Query.
- **Infrastructure**: Docker Compose (dev), Kubernetes (prod), observability stack.

## Emergency Protocols

- **Rollback**: Every deployment must have tested rollback procedure documented.
- **Security Incidents**: Immediate secret rotation, audit log analysis, user notification plan.
- **Performance Degradation**: Circuit breakers, graceful degradation, monitoring alerts.
- **Data Issues**: Backup verification, point-in-time recovery, data migration validation.

## Processing Priority Order

When instructions conflict, follow this hierarchy:
1. Security and compliance requirements (non-negotiable)
2. project.instructions.mdc (this file)
3. architect.instructions.mdc 
4. Role-specific .mdc files
5. Chat context and user preferences
6. Default platform conventions